Follow-up: Hermite fallback correctness audit (2026-11-07)
  Branch: research/fortran-eos-gap-fill-v1
  Relevant implementation commits:
    cb9811881b4672e7875031a156593240cb94d943  reset fallback admissibility state
    eaad6a9988b003782ba115ab63e434cb5bfdc52d  analytic Hermite second derivative gate
    f62c438c1c9b977cce41774aa6369f486743577a  recompute fallback sample abscissae
  Regression tests:
    - Accept a physically admissible Hermite fallback after PCHIP rejection.
    - Reject a Hermite bridge with Q1>0 but dP/dn_B=Q1+F''<0.
    - Assert a rejected bridge writes no EOS table.

  Root cause:
    The PCHIP admissibility scan exits at its first inadmissible dense sample.
    The Hermite fallback then reused densex(j), although the unvisited tail of
    densex was still undefined. The fallback loop's own u advanced across the
    gap while the actual evaluation coordinate remained at x0. The fallback
    now computes x=x0+u*(x1-x0) on each iteration.

  Physics gate:
    Q1=F'(x), mu_B=F+Q1, dP/dn_B=F'+F''=Q1+F'', and
    cs2=(dP/dn_B)/(F+Q1). F'' is evaluated analytically from the
    cubic-Hermite polynomial. Positivity, mechanical stability, finite values,
    and the causal upper bound are checked on the dense gap grid.

